    template that pulled a value from XCom), it is parsed into a dict at execution time.
    A string is first parsed as JSON and, if that fails, as a Python literal (the
    representation that Jinja produces when rendering a dict pulled from XCom). Anything
    that does not resolve to a mapping is rejected.
